{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>How… [beautiful].</b> After 'I will save you,' and this is the meaning of 'Here I am.' מה נאוו is from the nif'al binyan, from the root of וכי תאוה הוא לעיניך (Genesis 3:6). And one who says that the nun is a root letter is not correct, even though you will find this expression in the language of our Rabbis." "<b>Your Elohim reigns.</b> This is 'Here I am.'"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 52, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra's elliptic transition 'After I will save you' refers back to the immediately preceding verse (52:6); rendered tersely as he wrote it."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:10.173907340Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}